{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Vanavaccha (1st)","html":"<article id='thag1.13'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.13 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.13 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dutiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Two </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Vanavacchattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Vanavaccha (1st) </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Nīlabbhavaṇṇā rucirā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Glistening, they look like blue stormclouds, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sītavārī sucindharā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>with waters cool and streams so clear, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Indagopakasañchannā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and covered all in ladybugs: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>te selā ramayanti man”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>these rocky crags delight me! </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Vanavaccho thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
